{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":47,"end_line":12,"end_col":48,"message":"`read` needs file-read access, but `c` is the console capability.","code":"cap_mismatch:IO.FileRead","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"insert","after_line":7,"text":"  needs IO.FileRead"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":47,"end_line":12,"end_col":48,"text":"_cap_fileread"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":29,"end_line":12,"end_col":29,"text":", _cap_fileread : Cap(IO.FileRead)"}]},"labels":[{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":42,"end_line":12,"end_col":49,"message":"`read` needs `Cap(IO.FileRead)`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":10,"end_line":12,"end_col":11,"message":"`c` was bound here as `Cap(IO.Console)`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":10,"start_col":2,"end_line":10,"end_col":51,"message":"`Cap(IO.FileRead)` is named here, and the module declares no `needs IO.FileRead`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":9,"end_line":12,"end_col":30,"message":"`main` is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)` here"}],"notes":["`IO.Console` and `IO.FileRead` are both parts of `IO`; neither contains the other.","help: give `main` a `Cap(IO.FileRead)` parameter and pass it to `read`.","and add `needs IO.FileRead` to the module."]}
